refore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=5$, ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩.$" 13194139545750 17592186576411 false] [17592186265736 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{z})=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,9,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4) & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{9}}=\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{4}}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,9,4)+(y-9)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,9,4)+(z-4)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,9,4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)+\\frac{1}{6}(y-9)-\\frac{1}{4}(z-4) \\\\ w-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1 & =0 \\\\ 12(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{1}{4}z-w+1) & =12\\cdot 0 \\\\ 6x+2y-3z-12w+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545750 17592186576411 false] [17592186265736 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}