al as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}xz\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x/8-z}xz\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x/8-z}xz\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x/8-z}xz\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xz[y]_{y=0}^{y=2-x/8-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xz(2-\\frac{x}{8}-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2xz-\\frac{{x}^{2}z}{8}-x{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2xz-\\frac{{x}^{2}z}{8}-x{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2xz-\\frac{{x}^{2}z}{8}-x{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{[x{z}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{2}{z}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{x{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{x}{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(\\frac{2x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{48}]}_{x=0}^{x=4} \\\\  & =(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{64}{48})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545750 17592186576411 false] [17592186281383 1074 "![](images/b4/b4428666d80d78dfa3a4e754df7e5b33ee7ee4a8712c617b4cef5400a9ba494d.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-\\frac{x}{8}-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/61/61de9aa1f6230dafb68c99d1b6345ee49c30a6d2f3f4825e44e6032daac23335.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is